-- Source text: Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), Act No. 23 of 2005, as enacted, from the unofficial plain-text rendering No.-23-of-2005.txt.
-- (c) Government of Ireland. Oireachtas Copyright Material is reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas.
--
-- WHAT THIS MODULE IS.
-- How an enactment operates and is construed, in the computable parts of Parts 3 and 4 of the Interpretation Act 2005 (Ireland), and of the Schedule:
--   s 17      exercising powers and fixing a commencement day before the commencement;
--   s 18(b)   masculine and feminine, which turn on the date of an Act or an instrument;
--   s 18(d)   a child includes an adopted child, which turns on the date of the Act;
--   s 18(e)   distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane;
--   s 18(f)   a series described by its first and last members includes both;
--   s 18(g)   marginal notes, shoulder notes and headings are not part of the enactment, subject to s 7;
--   s 20(1)   a definition applies unless a contrary intention appears;
--   s 21(2)   the Schedule's Part 2 words apply only to an enactment that comes into operation after the commencement of this Act;
--   Sch Pt 2  "full age".
-- It imports ie-interpretation-time (for commencement) and ie-general (for s 7). Section 4(1) (contrary intention) is assumed absent unless a function says otherwise.
--
-- DAYS AND THE MOMENT WITHIN A DAY.
-- Where the Act speaks of "after the passing" and the passing is a day (s 15(1)), a thing on that same day cannot be placed before or after it,
-- because the Act fixes no time of day for the passing. Such a function refuses on that day and answers on every other.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`

§ `Named refusals`

-- src:159 | Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of Act. 17.—Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a day subsequent to the date of the passing of the Act, the following provisions apply:
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 17 (src:159)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 17 says "after the passing", and the Act fixes no time of day for the passing, so a thing on the same day is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 17 says \"after the passing\", and the Act fixes no time of day for the passing, so a thing on the same day is not answered"

-- src:173 | (f) Series description. Where a consecutive series is described by reference to the first and last in the series, the description shall be read as including the first and the last in the series;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(f) (src:173)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 18(f) describes a series by its first and last members, and a last member that precedes the first does not describe one` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 18(f) describes a series by its first and last members, and a last member that precedes the first does not describe one"

-- src:186 | (2) In an enactment which comes into operation after the commencement of this Act, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 2 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(2) (src:186)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing, so whether an enactment that came into operation on 1 January 2006 did so after this Act is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing, so whether an enactment that came into operation on 1 January 2006 did so after this Act is not answered"

-- src:251 | “full age”, in relation to a person, means the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "full age" (src:251)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Act fixes no time of day at which a person attains full age, so whether the person was of full age throughout that day is not answered` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Act fixes no time of day at which a person attains full age, so whether the person was of full age throughout that day is not answered"

§ `Section 17: exercise of statutory powers before the commencement of an Act`

DECLARE `Facts for section 17` HAS
    `the day on which the Act or provision is expressed to come into operation`   IS A DATE
    `the day of the passing of the Act`                                            IS A DATE
    `the day on which it comes into operation is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Act confers a power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing for the purposes of the Act or provision`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the making or doing of it is necessary or expedient to enable the Act or provision to have full force and effect immediately on its coming into operation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a restriction imposed by the Act forbids doing it on the day in question`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:159 | Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of Act. 17.—Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a day subsequent to the date of the passing of the Act, the following provisions apply:
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 17 (src:159)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts for section 17`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 17 applies` f MEANS
    f's `the day on which the Act or provision is expressed to come into operation` GREATER THAN f's `the day of the passing of the Act`

-- src:159 | Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of Act. 17.—Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a day subsequent to the date of the passing of the Act, the following provisions apply:
-- src:160 | (a) if the day on which the Act or the provision comes into operation is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner, the statutory instrument, act or thing whereby the day is fixed or ascertained may, subject to any restriction imposed by the Act, be made or done at any time after the passing of the Act;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 17(a) (src:159-160)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A `Facts for section 17`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the instrument, act or thing that fixes the day may be made or done on` d `, the facts being` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `section 17 applies` f THEN FALSE
           IF NOT f's `the day on which it comes into operation is to be fixed or ascertained in a particular manner` THEN FALSE
           IF f's `a restriction imposed by the Act forbids doing it on the day in question` THEN FALSE
           IF d GREATER THAN f's `the day of the passing of the Act` THEN TRUE
           IF d LESS THAN f's `the day of the passing of the Act`    THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `section 17 says "after the passing", and the Act fixes no time of day for the passing, so a thing on the same day is not answered`

-- src:159 | Exercise of statutory powers before commencement of Act. 17.—Where an Act or a provision of an Act is expressed to come into operation on a day subsequent to the date of the passing of the Act, the following provisions apply:
-- src:161 | (b) if, for the purposes of the Act or the provision, the Act confers a power to make a statutory instrument or do any act or thing, the making or doing of which is necessary or expedient to enable the Act or provision to have full force and effect immediately on its coming into operation, the power may, subject to any restriction imposed by the Act, be exercised at any time after the passing of the Act.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 17(b) (src:159, src:161)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A `Facts for section 17`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing may be exercised on` d `, the facts being` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `section 17 applies` f THEN FALSE
           IF NOT f's `the Act confers a power to make a statutory instrument or do an act or thing for the purposes of the Act or provision` THEN FALSE
           IF NOT f's `the making or doing of it is necessary or expedient to enable the Act or provision to have full force and effect immediately on its coming into operation` THEN FALSE
           IF f's `a restriction imposed by the Act forbids doing it on the day in question` THEN FALSE
           IF d GREATER THAN f's `the day of the passing of the Act` THEN TRUE
           IF d LESS THAN f's `the day of the passing of the Act`    THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE `section 17 says "after the passing", and the Act fixes no time of day for the passing, so a thing on the same day is not answered`

§ `Section 18(b): gender`

DECLARE `A gender a word imports` IS ONE OF
    masculine
    feminine

-- src:165 | (b) Gender.
-- src:166 | (i) A word importing the masculine gender shall be read as also importing the feminine gender;
-- src:167 | (ii) In an Act passed on or after 22 December 1993, and in a statutory instrument made after that date, a word importing the feminine gender shall be read as also importing the masculine gender;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(b) (src:165-167)
GIVEN g IS A `A gender a word imports`
      k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a word importing the` g `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` k `passed or made on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN masculine THEN TRUE
    WHEN feminine THEN
        CONSIDER k
        WHEN `an Act of the Oireachtas`                         THEN d AT LEAST YMD 1993 12 22
        WHEN `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` THEN d AT LEAST YMD 1993 12 22
        WHEN `a statutory instrument`                           THEN d GREATER THAN YMD 1993 12 22

§ `Section 18(d): a child includes an adopted child`

DECLARE `Facts about an adopted child` HAS
    `the day the Act was passed`                                                                    IS A DATE
    `the Act was passed after the passing of the Adoption Act 1976`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child was adopted by the person under the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998 or another enactment to be construed together with them` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child was adopted outside the State`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adoption is recognised by virtue of the law for the time being in force in the State`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:169 | (d) Adopted child. A reference, however expressed, to a child of a person shall be read as including—
-- src:170 | (i) in an Act passed after the passing of the Adoption Act 1976 a reference to a child adopted by the person under the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998 and every other enactment which is to be construed together with any of those Acts, or
-- src:171 | (ii) in an Act passed on or after 14 January 1988 (the commencement of section 3 of the Status of Children Act 1987 ), a child to whom subparagraph (i) relates or a child adopted outside the State whose adoption is recognised by virtue of the law for the time being in force in the State;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(d) (src:169-171)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts about an adopted child`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to a child of the person includes the adopted child` f MEANS
        (    f's `the Act was passed after the passing of the Adoption Act 1976`
         AND f's `the child was adopted by the person under the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998 or another enactment to be construed together with them`)
     OR (    f's `the day the Act was passed` AT LEAST YMD 1988 1 14
         AND (   f's `the child was adopted by the person under the Adoption Acts 1952 to 1998 or another enactment to be construed together with them`
              OR (    f's `the child was adopted outside the State`
                  AND f's `the adoption is recognised by virtue of the law for the time being in force in the State`)))

§ `Section 18(e): distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane`

DECLARE Point HAS
    `east of the origin` IS A NUMBER
    `north of the origin` IS A NUMBER
    `above the origin`   IS A NUMBER

-- src:172 | (e) Distance. A word or expression relating to the distance between two points and every reference to the distance from or to a point shall be read as relating or referring to such distance measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(e) (src:172)
GIVEN p IS A Point
      q IS A Point
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the distance between` p `and` q `within the meaning of section 18(e)` MEANS
    SQRT (  ((p's `east of the origin`  MINUS q's `east of the origin`)  TIMES (p's `east of the origin`  MINUS q's `east of the origin`))
          PLUS ((p's `north of the origin` MINUS q's `north of the origin`) TIMES (p's `north of the origin` MINUS q's `north of the origin`)))

§ `Section 18(f): a series described by its first and last includes the first and the last`

-- src:173 | (f) Series description. Where a consecutive series is described by reference to the first and last in the series, the description shall be read as including the first and the last in the series;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(f) (src:173)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      first IS A NUMBER
      last IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the number` n `is a member of the series from` first `to` last MEANS
    IF   last LESS THAN first
    THEN `section 18(f) describes a series by its first and last members, and a last member that precedes the first does not describe one`
    ELSE n AT LEAST first AND n AT MOST last

-- src:173 | (f) Series description. Where a consecutive series is described by reference to the first and last in the series, the description shall be read as including the first and the last in the series;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(f) (src:173)
GIVEN first IS A NUMBER
      last IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of members of the series from` first `to` last MEANS
    IF   last LESS THAN first
    THEN `section 18(f) describes a series by its first and last members, and a last member that precedes the first does not describe one`
    ELSE (last MINUS first) PLUS 1

§ `Section 18(g): marginal notes, shoulder notes, headings and cross-lines, subject to section 7`

DECLARE `A matter in or about an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision`
    `a shoulder note placed at the beginning of a section or other provision`
    `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions`
    `the text of a provision`

-- src:174 | (g) Marginal and shoulder notes, etc. Subject to section 7, none of the following shall be taken to be part of the enactment or be construed or judicially noticed in relation to the construction or interpretation of the enactment:
-- src:175 | (i) a marginal note placed at the side, or a shoulder note placed at the beginning, of a section or other provision to indicate the subject, contents or effect of the section or provision,
-- src:176 | (ii) a heading or cross-line placed in or at the head of or at the beginning of a Part, Chapter, section, or other provision or group of sections or provisions to indicate the subject, contents or effect of the Part, Chapter, section, provision or group;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(g) (src:174-176)
GIVEN m IS A `A matter in or about an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the matter is taken to be part of the enactment` m MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision`                               THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a shoulder note placed at the beginning of a section or other provision`                         THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions`   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the text of a provision`                                                                          THEN TRUE

-- src:120 | Supplemental provision to sections 5 and 6. 7.—(1) In construing a provision of an Act for the purposes of section 5 or 6 , a court may, notwithstanding section 18 (g), make use of all matters that accompany and are set out in—
-- src:174 | (g) Marginal and shoulder notes, etc. Subject to section 7, none of the following shall be taken to be part of the enactment or be construed or judicially noticed in relation to the construction or interpretation of the enactment:
-- src:175 | (i) a marginal note placed at the side, or a shoulder note placed at the beginning, of a section or other provision to indicate the subject, contents or effect of the section or provision,
-- src:176 | (ii) a heading or cross-line placed in or at the head of or at the beginning of a Part, Chapter, section, or other provision or group of sections or provisions to indicate the subject, contents or effect of the Part, Chapter, section, provision or group;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 18(g); s 7(1) (src:174-176, src:120)
GIVEN m IS A `A matter in or about an enactment`
      k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the matter may be construed or judicially noticed in construing the enactment` m k `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled` MEANS
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN `the text of a provision` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a marginal note placed at the side of a section or other provision`
         THEN `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` k `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`
    WHEN `a shoulder note placed at the beginning of a section or other provision`
         THEN `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` k `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`
    WHEN `a heading or cross-line of a Part, Chapter, section or other provision or group of provisions`
         THEN `section 7(1) lets a court make use of the matter notwithstanding section 18(g)` k `the court is construing a provision for the purposes of section 5 or 6` `the matter accompanies and is set out in the signed text as enrolled`

§ `Section 20(1): a definition or other interpretation provision applies unless a contrary intention appears`

-- src:181 | Interpretation provisions. 20.—(1) Where an enactment contains a definition or other interpretation provision, the provision shall be read as being applicable except in so far as the contrary intention appears in—
-- src:182 | (a) the enactment itself, or
-- src:183 | (b) the Act under which the enactment is made.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 20(1) (src:181-183)
GIVEN `the contrary intention appears in the enactment itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary intention appears in the Act under which the enactment is made` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definition or interpretation provision is read as applicable` `the contrary intention appears in the enactment itself` `the contrary intention appears in the Act under which the enactment is made` MEANS
    NOT (   `the contrary intention appears in the enactment itself`
         OR (CONSIDER `the contrary intention appears in the Act under which the enactment is made`
             WHEN NOTHING   THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST flag THEN flag))

§ `Section 21(2): the Schedule's Part 2 words apply to an enactment that comes into operation after the commencement of this Act`

-- "after" is strict. This Act comes into operation at the end of 31 December 2005 (s 1(2) with s 16(2)).
-- An enactment that comes into operation at the same moment (an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 January 2006) does not come into operation AFTER it.
-- An enactment whose only commencement day is a date of passing (s 16(1)) names no moment, so 1 January 2006 itself is not answered.

-- src:84 | (2) This Act comes into operation on 1 January 2006.
-- src:186 | (2) In an enactment which comes into operation after the commencement of this Act, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 2 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(2) (src:186); s 1(2) (src:84)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the enactment comes into operation after the commencement of this Act` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER (`the commencement of` facts)'s `the moment the text fixes`
    WHEN JUST m THEN m's `the day it ends` GREATER THAN (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `the facts about this Act`)'s `the day it ends`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        BRANCH IF (`the commencement of` facts)'s `the day the text names` GREATER THAN (`the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `the facts about this Act`) THEN TRUE
               IF (`the commencement of` facts)'s `the day the text names` LESS THAN (`the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `the facts about this Act`)    THEN FALSE
               OTHERWISE `section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing, so whether an enactment that came into operation on 1 January 2006 did so after this Act is not answered`

-- src:186 | (2) In an enactment which comes into operation after the commencement of this Act, a word or expression to which a particular meaning, construction or effect is assigned in Part 2 of the Schedule has the meaning, construction or effect so assigned to it.
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 s 21(2) (src:186)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` facts MEANS
    `the enactment comes into operation after the commencement of this Act` facts

§ `Schedule Part 2: "full age"`

-- "full age" means the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event.
-- The Act does not say how to find the day on which a person attains an age (it has no anniversary rule), so the two days are INPUTS, never computed from a date of birth.
-- NOTHING means the event has not happened.

DECLARE `Facts for full age` HAS
    `the day on which the person attained the age of 18 years` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the day on which the person married`                      IS A MAYBE DATE

-- src:251 | “full age”, in relation to a person, means the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "full age" (src:251)
GIVEN f IS A `Facts for full age`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day on which the person attains full age` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the day on which the person attained the age of 18 years`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN f's `the day on which the person married`
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER f's `the day on which the person married`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
        WHEN JUST m  THEN IF m LESS THAN a THEN JUST m ELSE JUST a

-- src:251 | “full age”, in relation to a person, means the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "full age" (src:251)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A `Facts for full age`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is of full age at the end of` d `, the facts being` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the person attains full age` f
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST e   THEN d AT LEAST e

-- src:251 | “full age”, in relation to a person, means the time when the person attains the age of 18 years or sooner marries, or any time after either event;
@ref Interpretation Act 2005 Schedule Pt 2 "full age" (src:251)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      f IS A `Facts for full age`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is of full age throughout` d `, the facts being` f MEANS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the person attains full age` f
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST e   THEN
        BRANCH IF d GREATER THAN e THEN TRUE
               IF d LESS THAN e    THEN FALSE
               OTHERWISE `the Act fixes no time of day at which a person attains full age, so whether the person was of full age throughout that day is not answered`
